@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+# GitHub Runner mode
+
+The Runner tab starts/resumes a selected macOS VM and asks the **existing Mac
+companion** to start GitHub's ARM64 runner. macOS and an unlocked user session
+are still necessary; this does not turn iOS into an Xcode host.
+
+1. In the Mac, install/update the companion once using Henge's Details → Sharing
+   setup command. A companion from an older IPA needs this update. Henge does
+   not blindly open Terminal and submit keystrokes: it cannot reliably identify
+   which guest application has focus.
+2. In Henge's Runner tab select the Mac and repository. For first registration,
+   paste the temporary token from GitHub Settings → Actions → Runners → New
+   self-hosted runner. Start. After registration, leave the token empty.
+3. Install Xcode and its tools inside this Mac for iOS builds. New workflows can
+   use `runs-on: [self-hosted, macOS, ARM64, henge]`. In this fork's existing
+   workflows, manually select `runner_mode: henge`. Push validation continues on
+   the cloud runner, so an offline iPad cannot block all development.
+
+The dashboard shows **listener process state**, not an inferred GitHub online
+state or job success. Check GitHub's runner/job page for those. The Mac companion
+downloads only an official `actions/runner` ARM64 asset whose SHA-256 matches
+the release's digest. Configuration uses an argument array and an environment
+token, not a shell-interpolated command. Token values are never preferences,
+shared-folder files, subprocess output in iOS logs, or status responses. GitHub
+stores its registered credentials in the private guest runner directory:
+`~/Library/Application Support/Henge/ActionsRunner`. A changed repository is
+rejected rather than silently replacing an existing registration. Guest jobs
+run with the user's account privileges, as with any self-hosted runner.
+
+The upstream `run.sh` signal-aware wrapper owns the listener and worker group,
+including self-update restarts. There is one serial runner owner, command
+revision, bounded guest HTTP mailbox, cancellation path and status heartbeat.
+Old-session status reports cannot update a new session. No second launchd
+daemon or repeating Swift timer is introduced. Errors stop startup instead of
+looping downloads/registration. Guest `_diag` logs contain detailed failures. A configured runner with damaged
+binaries is preserved and reported for explicit recovery instead of overwriting
+its credentials.
+
+While the dashboard is visible, Henge detaches the **local presentation layer**.
+The existing renderer retains its current surface; showing the desktop
+reattaches it and presents the latest frame. Guest rendering, Retina, resolution,
+external monitors and port-one Henge Link retain their existing paths. This
+eliminates local drawable/presentation work in runner view; it does not eliminate
+macOS CPU/GPU work or demonstrate a device temperature reduction.
+
+## Background execution and PiP
+
+Background processing is explicit and off initially. On iOS 26+, Henge checks
+hardware GPU support **and the entitlement on the installed signature**, then
+requests `BGContinuedProcessingTaskRequest` with `.gpu` and fail-if-unavailable.
+Only an attached task permits the VM to continue after leaving Henge. Cancellation
+or expiration revokes that permission and queues a real pause, with the existing
+optional Instant Resume save. CPU/GPU quiescence uses the existing serial
+pause/save/continue owner. Returning to Henge resumes through that same queue.
+The boot RAM value is now assigned so an enabled background snapshot is actually
+eligible to save. Startup now selects the real native restore path for a valid
+saved Mac, rather than always cold-booting. Invalid build/settings saves are
+rejected with explicit discard-and-start recovery. Snapshot identity and restore
+use the actual saved display dimensions, preserving them across a fold/window
+change.
+
+The normal/personal signing entitlements are preserved. The user's logs show no
+signed continued-processing GPU entitlement. **This ordinary IPA therefore
+cannot promise background VM execution.** It reports the missing capability
+and force-pauses Runner mode even if persistent Instant Resume is off. Keep
+Henge visible, or use iPad Split View. iOS may terminate the app or end a task;
+neither this API nor a PiP window provides an unlimited server lifetime.
+
+No fake audio/video keepalive or static PiP window is added. AVKit PiP accepts
+video sample-buffer content, but does not grant the separate GPU entitlement
+needed by this Metal VM. A new live capture/encode path would add GPU work
+without resolving the missing execution permission on this installation. A
+future genuine remote-desktop PiP viewer can be added independently if useful.
+
+## Verification
+
+`make test-runner` exercises the real guest HTTP mailbox and a real child runner
+process using an isolated fake runner directory: retry, status bounds, secret
+retirement, stop/cancellation, repository mismatch and stale session rejection.
+DisplayRouter regression covers hidden output, refresh/replacement while hidden
+and restoring the newest layer. Existing native lifecycle/snapshot and sanitizer
+checks remain mandatory, followed by full iOS SDK/app compilation.
+
+Cloud tests cannot validate this device's GPU grant, iOS expiration timing,
+actual GitHub registration with the user's temporary token, or thermal behaviour.
+Those remain clearly separate from process/control correctness and compilation.
